@page "/components/bottom-menu"

<PageTitle>Bottom Menu — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Bottom Menu</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    useLayouts' bottom menu: a bar of icon buttons, each opening its own panel above the bar.
    Moving from one button to the next morphs the panel to the new size and blurs the new content
    in, with Motion.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Basic</h2>
<Example Source="BottomMenuExample.razor"><BottomMenuExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">What the platform does</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Every panel is a <code>[popover]</code> and every button names its panel with
    <code>popovertarget</code>, so one panel is open at a time, a click outside closes it and so
    does Escape — the three things upstream wires by hand. That also means the menu opens and
    closes with scripting off; only the placement above the bar and the motion need ui.js.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Writing items</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    <code>IconContent</code> is what the bar shows, <code>Label</code> names the button for a screen
    reader and <code>ChildContent</code> is the panel. <code>Value</code> is required: the item is
    rendered twice, once as a button and once as a panel, and the two find each other by it. An
    item with no <code>ChildContent</code> is a plain button with nothing to open.
</p>
